te(kws, limit=1450, minlen=25):\n    best = None\n    for p in sorted(TXT):\n        t = TXT[p]\n        occs = []\n        for k in kws:\n            occs += [(s, e, k) for s, e in occur(t, k)]\n        if not occs: continue\n        occs.sort()\n        # sliding window\n        for i in range(len(occs)):\n            covered = set()\n            j = i\n            while j < len(occs) and len(covered) < len(kws):\n                covered.add(occs[j][2]); j += 1\n            if len(covered) < len(kws): break\n            seg = (occs[i][0], occs[j-1][1])\n            if best is None or (seg[1]-seg[0]) < (best[2]-best[1]) ... \n```\nSimplify: track best as (page, start, end). Compute candidate length; keep min length but require expanded length >= minlen.\n\nThen expansion function.\n\ndef expand(t, s, e):\n    lo = max(0, s - 300)\n    # sentence start\n    k = s\n    while k > lo:\n        if t[k-1] in \".!?\" and t[k:k+1] in \" \\n\\t\":\n            break\n        k -= 1\n    start = k\n    hi = min(len(t), e + 300)\n    k2 = e\n    while k2 < hi:\n        if t[k2] in \".!?\" :\n            k2 += 1\n            break\n        k2 += 1\n    end = k2\n    q = re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", t[start:end]).strip()\n    return q\n\nThen truncate to limit keeping keyword coverage: just slice q[:limit] then rstrip; ensure len>=minlen.\n\nOk. I'll write everything and print results as diagnostics.\n\nThen:\n\nreport = {...}\n\ncontent = json.dumps(report, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\nh = read_file('report.json')['file_hash']\nprint(write_file('report.json', content, h)['file_hash'] if ... )\n\nActually write_file returns dict; check rc? It returns something; just print.\n\nThen run pytest, print rc/stdout, and if rc==0 → final_answer.\n\nLet's assemble Chinese strings (must be careful with quotes inside JSON — fine).\n\nWrite code now.\n\nEvidence objects: {\"question\": field, \"page\": p, \"quote\": q}.\n\nNeed quote for each of 10 fields. If find_quote returns None for some